# Hestia-MediaManager .gitignore
# What's allowed in the repo: source code, Dockerfiles, requirements,
# the Makefile, and docs. Everything else listed below is either a
# build artefact, a Python/Node cache, or runtime data that contains
# user secrets (Plex tokens) or library contents.

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
venv/
.venv/
env/
.env

# ── Node / frontend build ──────────────────────────────────────────
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
frontend/.vite/

# ── User runtime data (NEVER commit) ───────────────────────────────
# Contains your Plex token and registered server credentials.
server_data/
# Explicit - already covered by server_data/ above, but called out
# so a deployment that flattens the directory rule still keeps the
# encryption key (server/secrets.py) private to the host volume.
server_data/.keyfile

# Per-run logs and snapshots. May contain server URLs, library names,
# file paths, and other library-shape information. Keep local.
plex_logs/
snapshots/
# Legacy directory from before the PR-13 rename; kept here so an
# operator who didn't run the auto-migration doesn't accidentally
# commit a directory of old .plexbackup.json files.
plex_exports/

# Snapshot / export payloads written by the engine. May land in the
# repo root (loose runs, chained-transfer temp files) as well as in
# the snapshots/ dir above. Both the legacy .plexbackup.json name and
# the current .plexexport.json name (PR-13 rename) are covered, plus
# the .tmp.* chained-fallback files server/direct_transfer.py leaves
# behind on import failure.
/*.plexbackup.json
*.tmp.plexbackup.json
*.plexexport.json
*.tmp.plexexport.json
# Explorer / browser "duplicate download" copies insert " (N)" BEFORE
# the final .json, so the name ends in "(1).json" not ".plexexport.json"
# and the rules above miss it. Catch those too.
*.plexexport (*).json
*.plexbackup (*).json

# Engine run-output archives. The snapshot / direct / fan-out engines
# write a ``run_<server>_<libraries>_<timestamp>.zip`` of a completed
# run, often into the repo root. Generated artefacts, never source.
run_*.zip

# Loose media / scratch files dropped at the repo root - screenshots,
# screen recordings, stray downloads. Anchored with a leading slash so
# real image assets under frontend/ are NOT affected.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.webp
/*.bmp
/*.mp4
/*.webm
/*.mov
/*.avi

# SQLite databases - media.db, snapshots.db, the auth DB, and the
# per-server snapshot .db files. All are runtime data: library
# contents, watch history, and (for the auth / managed-user tables)
# encrypted credentials. None of these should ever be committed.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Per-run engine logs. setup_logging() writes runtime.log / errors.log
# / media.log / troubleshoot.log (and Explorer-style "runtime (1).log"
# duplicates) into the working directory. They carry server URLs,
# library names, and file paths - keep them local.
*.log

# ── IDE / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.history/

# ── Editor / file-manager duplicates ───────────────────────────────
# Catches accidental copies like "README copy.md" (Finder) and
# "README - Copy.md" (Windows Explorer) so they don't end up in git.
* copy.*
* copy *.*
*-copy.*
* - Copy.*
* - Copy (*).*

# ── Docker ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docker-compose.yml itself IS tracked. These are local-only:
docker-compose.override.yml
.env.local

# ── Dev blog (temporarily excluded from git pre-v0.18.0) ──────────
# The dev blog HTML lives at frontend/public/dev-blog/ and is served
# by Vite at /dev-blog/ when the in-app tab is enabled. Operator is
# doing personal-cleanup polish before public exposure; the tab is
# also commented out in frontend/src/App.tsx for this release.
# Remove this block when the blog is ready to ship publicly.
frontend/public/dev-blog/

# ── Dev-only utilities not part of the shipped product ────────────
# Standalone CLI fidelity scanner: referenced by dev_docs/QA_CHECKLIST
# §19 but not wired into the in-app surface. Useful for operator-side
# spot-checks of snapshot databases, not for end users.
tools/

# Experimental sidecar-application scaffolding (currently empty
# placeholder; not part of v0.18.0).
sidecar-applications/

# Root-level HTML files at repo root are operator-internal review
# docs (e.g. TEST_RESULTS_AND_NEXT_STEPS.html). The /*.md rule above
# excludes root markdown with explicit !README/!QUICKSTART/etc.
# allowances; this rule does the same for root HTML.
/*.html

# ── Local-only dev scaffolding (NOT for the repo) ──────────────────
# Everything host-only lives under dev_docs/: developer working-notes,
# the backend unit-test suite (dev_docs/tests_backend/), its
# requirements-dev.txt, sample data/logs, reviews, specs, and the
# CHANGELOG. None of it is part of the shipped product.
dev_docs/

# Multi-agent coordination workspace. Holds per-agent scope files
# and the shared claudeagentwork.md handoff log; only meaningful to
# the local agent runtime, never shipped.
agent-context/

# Per-project state directory for the local agent runtime (settings
# for permissions / tools). Host-only, never part of the shipped
# product.
.claude/

# Root-level test directories. The multi-agent coordination put
# tests_backend/ (shared territory) + tests_live/ + tests_structural/
# at the repo root; per the local-only-dev-scaffolding policy above,
# they stay local. The 4 historically-tracked files are removed from
# the index via `git rm --cached` so a fresh clone never sees them.
tests_backend/
tests_live/
tests_structural/

# Root-level Markdown is local-only working/dev docs (design notes,
# etc.) EXCEPT the shipped docs. Add a new doc at the repo root
# and it stays local unless it's explicitly un-ignored below.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/SOURCES.md
!/QUICKSTART.md
!/OVERVIEW.md

# E2E test harness isolated data directory. Created by Playwright
# globalSetup, wiped by globalTeardown. The bind-mount target for the
# e2e docker compose override (dev_docs/tests_e2e/docker-compose.e2e.yml).
dev_docs/tests_e2e/.e2e-data/
dev_docs/tests_e2e/.stack-owned-by-e2e

# Scratch / one-shot operational scripts at the repo root. The session
# that wrote M0-M8 produced tmp_*.py move scripts, tmp_*.txt suite logs,
# and a one-shot cleanup_test_contamination.py. These are not app code;
# the engineering history lives in dev_docs/process/changelog.md.
/tmp_*.py
/tmp_*.txt
/cleanup_*.py

# Backup database files (created by cleanup scripts before destructive
# DELETEs). Same family as the .db.bak / .keyfile rules above; these
# carry a timestamp suffix like .db.bak-20260530-092535 so they need
# their own pattern.
/server_data/*.db.bak-*

# Root-level Plex snapshot artifacts. Snapshots are user data, never
# app code. The shipped path puts them under ./snapshots/, but
# operator runs sometimes land .db / .plexexport.json at the repo root
# (drag-drop, manual download). Ignore both shapes at root only; the
# ./snapshots/ tree is already ignored via the snapshots/ rule.
/*.db
/*.plexexport.json

# Root-level HTML review documents (POSTGRES_MIGRATION_REVIEW.html,
# TEST_RESULTS_AND_NEXT_STEPS.html, TEST_REVIEW_PRE_RELEASE.html and
# similar). These are local dev notes, not shipped app surface.
/*.html
